king_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Give an anchored grep target (a required phrase or heading) for AC1/AC3/AC8, e.g. `grep -q 'bounded in wall-clock time' AGENTS.md`, so each guidance criterion has a concrete proving command like AC2.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5d","T5e"],"criteria":["E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.5375,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC1: 'Verified by the text being present in AGENTS.md.'","AC3: 'Verified by the text in AGENTS.md.'","AC2 by contrast names checkable literals ('timeout 120', \"trap 'kill 0' EXIT INT TERM\"), giving an anchored grep target."],"finding":"The prose-intent guidance criteria (AC1, AC3, AC8) are verified only by 'the text being present in AGENTS.md' with no anchored grep string, unlike AC2 which names concrete literals; 'states that...' / 'forbids...' is a subjective presence check.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fcabd8f30be41893d","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria AC1, AC3, AC8","norm_id":"neec748aeec09fd51","priority":0.4125,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer cannot mechanically confirm 'forbids PPID-1 orphans' is present because no exact phrase/anchor is specified."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["vague/subjective terms present: sufficient"],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State how the orphaned-load detection behaves on non-Unix supported platforms (e.g. Windows, where PID 1 is not init): either define a platform-appropriate orphan signal or explicitly scope the check to POSIX and say so, and clarify how `--include-system` path-exclusion is defined per-platform.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5a","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.portability"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'A detection check reports compute processes whose parent is PID 1'","Plan evidence is entirely macOS-specific (launchd, WindowServer, JamfDaemon, Virtualization VM) and the operator note uses `pkill`","Windows has no PID-1 init reaper; orphan re-parenting semantics differ, so a PPID==1 filter never matches"],"finding":"The detection check's core signal — 'compute processes whose parent is PID 1' — is a POSIX/Unix assumption. On Windows there is no init process at PID 1 and orphaned processes are not re-parented to PID 1, so the real adapter would flag nothing and the capability is a silent no-op on that platform.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f671f26f0abb7cff2","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — 'compute processes whose parent is PID 1 and whose accumulated CPU time exceeds 3600 CPU-seconds'","norm_id":"nee4f3e73746f9ddc","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Windows platform (developer workstation or CI runner): `python scripts/check_orphaned_load.py` runs, the PPID==1 filter matches nothing, and a genuinely leaked orphaned load generator is never reported — the check appears green while the defect persists.","macOS `--include-system` path-exclusion logic (launchd/system paths) has no equivalent definition on Linux/Windows, so `--include-system`/default filtering behaves inconsistently across platforms."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add an AC scoping the check to POSIX hosts (documenting the PID-1/init assumption) or define a portable orphan/system-path abstraction; note that the `pkill` operator remediation is POSIX-only.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the PPID-1 platform assumption in AC 4 (orphans reparent to PID 1 on macOS / no-subreaper Linux) and either scope the check to that environment or broaden the orphan signal to also catch subreaper-reparented compute processes.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC 4: 'A detection check reports compute processes whose parent is PID 1 and whose accumulated CPU time exceeds 3600 CPU-seconds'","AC 4: 'Runnable on demand as a plain command with no dependency on any CI provider (project.portability)'","ABSENCE: no statement that PPID-1 is a macOS/no-subreaper assumption, nor how detection degrades where orphans reparent to a subreaper rather than PID 1"],"finding":"The detection mechanism keys on 'parent is PID 1' as the orphan signal, but never states the platform assumption behind it. On the affected macOS host orphans reparent to launchd (PID 1), so it holds there; but the plan also requires portability ('no dependency on any CI provider', project.portability). On Linux under a subreaper (systemd user session, or a harness that called PR_SET_CHILD_SUBREAPER) an orphaned worker reparents to the subreaper PID, not 1 — so the check would silently miss exactly the leaked-generator class it targets.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3906de9196486a84","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, AC 4 ('compute processes whose parent is PID 1')","norm_id":"n181d00b035758a89","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A subagent leaks a 'while True: pass' burner inside a systemd user session on a Linux CI/dev host; the orphan reparents to the session subreaper, PPID != 1, and the sweep reports nothing."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"ve